# Keep secrets out of the image. The build does `COPY . .`, and a .env copied
# into a layer stays in that layer forever — `rm` in a later step does not
# remove it, and anyone who can pull the image can read it. Production gets its
# configuration from the environment, never from a file in the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Installed per-platform inside the image. Copying the host's would drop
# Windows or macOS binaries into a Linux container.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Stale .next from the host would be copied over and then
# partially overwritten, which is a genuinely confusing way to fail.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local state that is not part of the application.
.pgdata
.uploads
phase0/out

.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
*.log

# Documentation does not change behaviour, and leaving it out keeps the build
# cache from being invalidated by a typo fix in the runbook.
docs
*.md
!phase0/README.md
